                <pb facs="0468" n="461" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg461"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9660: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-24T14:00:00+08:00">August 24, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:04 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>547. In an interview granted today to Reuters aboard Japanese flagship, Admiral
                    Hasegawa made the following statement which the Japanese Consul General
                    confirms: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“It has been the intention of the Japanese Government to localize the
                            Sino-Japanese conflict and to bring about ultimately closer and better
                            relations with China. However, with the situation aggravated by Chinese
                            to such an extent as it is, we deem it important that a safety zone
                            should be established in and around Shanghai, and that all causes of
                            further trouble should be removed once and for all.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
